1
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:06,040
Using Language Reading

2
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:09,780
Showing Our Feelings

3
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:17,100
Body language is one of the most powerful means of communication, often even more powerful

4
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:18,700
than spoken language.

5
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:22,840
People around the world show all kinds of feelings,

6
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:26,460
wishes and attitudes that they might never speak aloud.

7
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:30,720
It is possible to "read" others around us,

8
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:35,480
even if they do not intend for us to catch their unspoken communication.

9
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:39,960
Of course, body language can be misread,

10
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:43,940
but many gestures and actions are universal.

11
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:48,520
The most universal facial expression is,

12
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:56,320
of course, the smile – its function is to show happiness and put people at ease.

13
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:59,500
It does not always mean that we are truly happy,

14
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:00,100
however.

15
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,740
Smiles around the world can be false,

16
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:06,800
hiding other feelings like anger,

17
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:08,760
fear or worry.

18
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:15,180
There are unhappy smiles, such as when someone "loses face"

19
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:17,340
and smiles to hide it.

20
00:01:17,340 --> 00:01:22,840
However, the general purpose of smiling is to show good feelings.

21
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:29,180
From the time we are babies, we show unhappiness or anger by frowning.

22
00:01:30,140 --> 00:01:31,940
In most places around the world,

23
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:36,060
frowning and turning one's back to someone shows anger.

24
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:42,260
Making a fist and shaking it almost always means that someone is angry

25
00:01:42,260 --> 00:01:44,120
and threatening another person.

26
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:48,780
There are many ways around the world to show agreement,

27
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:53,120
but nodding the head up and down is used for agreement,

28
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,540
almost worldwide.

29
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:03,480
Most people also understand that shaking the head from side to side means disagreement or refusal.

30
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,440
How about showing that I am bored?

31
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:11,740
Looking away from people or yawning will,

32
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:15,300
in most cases, make me appear to be uninterested.

33
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:20,360
However, if I turn toward and look at someone or something,

34
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:25,100
people from almost every culture will think that I am interested.

35
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:28,760
If I roll my eyes and turn my head away,

36
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:33,920
I most likely do not believe what I am hearing or do not like it.

37
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:37,080
Being respectful to people is subjective,

38
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:44,840
based on each culture, but in general it is probably not a good idea to give a hug to a boss or teacher.

39
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:52,720
In almost every culture, it is not usually good to stand too close to someone of a higher rank.

40
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:58,700
Standing at a little distance with open hands will show that I am willing to listen.

41
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:02,880
With so many cultural differences between people,

42
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:06,600
it is great to have some similarities in body language.

43
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:10,020
We can often be wrong about each other,

44
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:15,380
so it is an amazing thing that we understand each other as well as we do!
